losed_at":"2026-06-19T16:54:35Z"},"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-02-28T12:08:41Z","updated_at":"2026-03-12T14:13:34Z","closed_at":"2026-03-12T14:13:34Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.6\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8183) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10750H CPU @ 2.60GHz (12 threads) - 15.84 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIt seems similar to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/75050.\n\nBasically `EditorPlugin._forward_3d_draw_over_viewport(overlay)` is not called when the camera is panned or rotated, while it seems to be updated when camera is zoomed.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/2q9lPzk0AY8\n\nTo add `set_force_draw_over_forwarding_enabled()` to the `enter_tree()` of the plug-in does not work.\n\nHowever, the overlay does update when dragging the gizmo handles.\n\nMy understanding is either is should be called for all camera movements, or for none.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nMake a GizmoEditorPlugin and try to use `EditorPlugin._forward_3d_draw_over_viewport(overlay)` to display circles on top of the handles. Rotate the camera.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nCan provide one if requested.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{